RAMFS - public domain
=====================

The original RAMFS (Karl Olsen, with later versions maintained by Andrew Belov; version 1.21, 2006) was released by its
authors as freeware / public domain: see readme.txt ("RAMFS is freeware. Feel free to use it, and to get ideas from the
source code when you develop your own file systems") and the README of the original repository ("LICENSE: Public Domain").

The changes and additions of the OS2World update (version 1.22) are released into the public domain as well. This covers
the build files, src\ifslib.c, src\os2compat.h, the changes to the original sources, the replacement kernel interface
headers src\fsd.h and src\fsh.h (see doc\PROVENANCE.md), the test scripts and the documentation.

Where the law of a country does not allow a public domain dedication, everyone may use, copy, change and distribute this
software for any purpose, without restriction and without any warranty.

THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND.
